  "138": {
    "inputs": {
      "value": "Create a 10-second video using the two images as visual references.\n\nCRITICAL TIMING REQUIREMENT:\nThe video must START on a completely black screen and END on a completely black screen, with visible fade-in and fade-out transitions.\n\nReference image 1 defines the DAYTIME appearance.\nReference image 2 defines the NIGHTTIME appearance.\nThese references represent intermediate states within the video. They do not define the opening or closing frame.\n\nFollow this exact chronological sequence:\n\n00:00.000–00:01.000 — BLACK TO DAY FADE\nBegin with a completely black screen. Keep the entire frame pure black for the first 0.15 seconds. Then smoothly fade in the daytime scene, reaching the full appearance of reference image 1 at exactly 1.00 second. This is an editorial fade from black, achieved by gradually increasing the visibility of the whole image.\n\n00:01.000–00:03.000 — STATIC DAYTIME HOLD\nHold the fully visible daytime scene completely still for two seconds. Maintain constant daylight and exposure.\n\n00:03.000–00:07.000 — DAY TO NIGHT TRANSITION\nOver four seconds, smoothly and continuously transition from the daytime appearance of reference image 1 to the nighttime appearance of reference image 2. Daylight gradually dims, the sky darkens, and the nighttime stars gradually appear. Reach the complete nighttime appearance at exactly 7.00 seconds. Preserve the same scene geometry throughout.\n\n00:07.000–00:09.000 — STATIC NIGHTTIME HOLD\nHold the fully visible nighttime scene completely still for two seconds, with constant nighttime exposure and stationary stars.\n\n00:09.000–00:10.000 — NIGHT TO BLACK FADE\nSmoothly fade out the ENTIRE nighttime image into complete blackness. Reach pure black by 9.85 seconds and keep the entire screen completely black until the video ends at 10.00 seconds. No scene details, stars or silhouettes remain visible.\n\nVISUAL CONSISTENCY:\nOne continuous locked-off composition. Preserve the reference framing, perspective, 16:9 canvas and existing letterbox bars. Every building, roof, palisade, wagon, tent and tree remains stationary and spatially consistent. Only lighting, sky appearance and the opening/closing fade opacity change. No camera movement, zoom, cuts, object motion or geometry morphing.\n\nFINAL CHECK:\nOpening frame: pure black.\nAt 1 second: full daytime.\nAt 3 seconds: daytime transition begins.\nAt 7 seconds: full nighttime.\nAt 9 seconds: closing fade begins.\nFinal frame: pure black.\n\nAudio: silent, no music or sound effects."
    },
    "class_type": "PrimitiveStringMultiline",
    "_meta": {
      "title": "Input Text (Prompt)",
      "cnr_id": "comfy-core",
      "ver": "0.33.0"
    }
